WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:05.410
"Thor: Love and Thunder" has double the Thor
action with Jane Foster joining Odin's son

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:10.000
– but for many fans, the real star of the
show is the man who's trying to burn it all

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.000
down.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.920
Warning: spoilers for "Thor: Love and Thunder"
ahead.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:18.970
In Marvel movies, the hero is typically only
as good as the villain they have to go up

00:00:18.970 --> 00:00:19.970
against.

00:00:19.970 --> 00:00:24.359
And in "Thor: Love and Thunder," we see the
god of thunder battle one of his most imposing

00:00:24.359 --> 00:00:25.710
foes to date.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:29.670
In the past, Thor's biggest battles have often
been family affairs.

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:35.290
With the exception of Malekith the Dark Elf
and Thanos the Mad Titan, Thor has spent most

00:00:35.290 --> 00:00:39.430
of his time battling his siblings, namely
Loki and Hela.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:43.750
He even had his issues with his father, before
he grew up a little and proved himself to

00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:44.750
be worthy.

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:49.300
But now, he needs some fresh blood to go up
against, and he gets it in the form of Gorr

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:50.650
the God Butcher.

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:53.310
Gorr's issue with Thor is fairly straightforward.

00:00:53.310 --> 00:00:58.379
He felt betrayed by his own god, so once he
got hold of the Necrosword, he vowed to kill

00:00:58.379 --> 00:01:00.329
every god out there.

00:01:00.329 --> 00:01:04.700
Thor is no exception, and based on some of
the scenes we get, he's pretty efficient in

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.300
his god-killing.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:11.360
He manages to defeat some truly formidable
foes before turning his attention to Eternity

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:15.540
and getting that coveted wish to take out
every god once and for all.

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:20.070
He may be the bad guy, but he's more than
made his mark on fans, who can't help but

00:01:20.070 --> 00:01:24.050
praise what's arguably one of the best villains
in a Marvel movie ever.

00:01:24.050 --> 00:01:28.920
"Thor: Love and Thunder" opens with a sequence
showing Gorr's tragic backstory as he wanders

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:31.350
the desert with his daughter, doomed to die.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:35.540
When he finally stumbles upon his god, he's
heartbroken to realize that the god doesn't

00:01:35.540 --> 00:01:38.010
care about him or his dead daughter.

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:42.120
In response, he vows to kill every god out
there for revenge.

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:43.890
It's a heartbreaking sequence.

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:47.210
Who can't empathize with a man who's just
lost his daughter?

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:51.350
And fans seem to think this makes Gorr one
of the better antagonists to come out of Marvel

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:52.460
Studios.

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:55.090
One Redditor kicked off a discussion on the
topic, saying,

00:01:55.090 --> 00:02:00.530
"This was the first time, in a verrry long
time, that I actually felt the menace of the

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:02.430
villain and jeopardy of the characters.

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:07.010
And it was the first time I felt that I wanted
to see more of the villain's adventures."

00:02:07.010 --> 00:02:11.420
A ton of people agreed, with many wishing
they had gotten to see more of Gorr in the

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:12.420
flick.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:13.600
One user stated,

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:18.010
"Definitely wish we could have seen at least
one more scene of God Butchery."

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:22.200
There may very well be more Gorr moments on
the horizon, somewhere in the special features

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:24.130
of the movie's home release.

00:02:24.130 --> 00:02:28.480
In an interview with IGN, Bale mentioned how
one particular scene had to be left on the

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:33.860
cutting room floor, potentially for being
a little bit too "extreme" – so anyone hoping

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:38.210
for more god butchery may well get their wish
granted in the months to come.

00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:40.690
"I'm counting on that."

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:45.390
Gorr likely won't come back to the MCU anytime
soon for another adventure, considering the

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:50.190
film's ending, but deleted scenes would be
more than welcome if it means fans can spend

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:54.440
a little bit more time with the surprisingly
compelling God Butcher.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:58.910
In "Thor: Love and Thunder," Gorr's health
gradually deteriorates due to his use of the

00:02:58.910 --> 00:02:59.960
Necrosword.

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:04.800
By the time he reaches Eternity, he's nearly
at death's door, and with his final promised

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:07.319
wish, he brings his daughter back to life.

00:03:07.319 --> 00:03:10.290
At the end of the day, Gorr's really just
a family man.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:14.840
He just wanted his family to be safe, which
is par the course for the Gorr readers know

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.360
from the comics.

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:19.700
Gorr's comic origin story is similar to the
one we see in the film.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:24.100
While he initially believes in the worthiness
of the gods, he soon loses hope due to the

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:26.400
loss of his wife and children.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:31.070
Unlike the film, his final child is a boy
in the comics, but his faith isn't enough,

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:33.360
and his child quickly perishes.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:36.280
Gorr is a relatively new addition to comics
lore.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:42.210
He made his first appearance in "Thor: God
of Thunder #2" in 2012, and he's gone on to

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:45.500
have numerous spars with the likes of the
Asgardian.

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:49.600
For those wishing for more adventures with
Gorr, the pages of a comic will be your best

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:50.600
bet.

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:54.610
There are plenty of folks who would like to
see more of the antagonist, as evidenced by

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:56.080
one Redditor, who wrote,

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:58.490
"Honestly I could watch a Gorr movie.

00:03:58.490 --> 00:04:01.260
Just the opening with his daughter made me
sympathize with him.

00:04:01.260 --> 00:04:02.980
Such an interesting character."

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:07.230
Gorr's return to the MCU is unlikely, despite
characters having come back from the dead

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:08.380
before.

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:13.130
But if you want more Gorr, you'll have to
head over to your local comic shop.

